\item \points{2c} \textbf{Backpropagation}

Using the same weights, bias and input vector as in part (b), first compute the loss value $L$. Then, perform backpropagation to compute gradients $\frac{\partial L}{\partial \mathbf{W}^{(1)}}$, $\frac{\partial L}{\partial \mathbf{b}^{(1)}}$, $\frac{\partial L}{\partial \mathbf{W}^{(2)}}$, and $\frac{\partial L}{\partial b^{(2)}}$. Assume the true label is $y_{\text{true}} = 0$ (negative sentiment) and we're using binary cross-entropy loss:
$$L = -[y_{\text{true}} \log(\hat{y}) + (1 - y_{\text{true}}) \log(1 - \hat{y})]$$

